1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
That clicking sound
when you turn the wheel?

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,000
That's not nothing.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,600
It's usually the CV joint —

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
the part that lets your axle
turn and flex at the same time.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,200
The rubber boot around it cracked.

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,600
Grease leaked out.

7
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,000
Now it's grinding metal
on metal every turn.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Ignore it long enough and
the joint fails completely —

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
that wheel stops taking power.

10
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Hear a click turning corners? Send this
to whoever's car makes that sound.
Nick's Tire and Auto — link in bio.
